{"name":"Happy Days","hex":"#506e82","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"happy days","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["An exclamation which expresses satisfaction."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/happy_days"}],"entries":[{"title":"Happy Days","blocks":[{"text":"Happy Days is an American television sitcom that aired on ABC from January 15, 1974 to July 19, 1984 with a total of 255 half-hour episodes spanning 11 seasons. Created by Garry Marshall, it was one of the most successful series of the 1970s. The series presented life in the 1950s and early 1960s Midwestern United States, where it also featured an ensemble cast, starring Ron Howard as Richie Cunningham, Henry Winkler as his friend Fonzie and Tom Bosley and Marion Ross as Richie's parents, Howard and Marion Cunningham. Although it opened to mixed reviews from critics, Happy Days became successful and popular over time."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Happy_Days_%28Miller-Boyett%29_original_logo.svg/330px-Happy_Days_%28Miller-Boyett%29_original_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Happy_Days","wikidata":"Q518589"},{"title":"Happy Days (play)","blocks":[{"text":"Happy Days is a play in two acts, written by Samuel Beckett first performed in 1961. Viewed positively by critics, it was named in The Independent as one of the 40 best plays of all time."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Sketch_of_scene_in_Happy_Days_%28play%29_by_Samuel_Beckett.jpg/330px-Sketch_of_scene_in_Happy_Days_%28play%29_by_Samuel_Beckett.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Happy_Days_(play)","wikidata":"Q1189196"},{"title":"Day","blocks":[{"text":"A day is the time period of a full rotation of the Earth with respect to the Sun. On average, this is 24 hours. As a 